      "id": "rel72g0",
      "content": "<strong>CHAPTER  12\tCLOCKS &amp; CALENDARS</strong>"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "c7i8mds",
      "content": "<em>Clock Angles | Coincidence | Calendar — Odd Days</em>"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "5xy6a8r",
      "content": "<strong>12.1  Clock Problems</strong>"
    },
    {
      "id": "32xj17y",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>CLOCK FUNDAMENTALS</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Clock has 360° total. 12 hours = 360°, so 1 hour = 30°.</p><p>Minute hand moves 360° in 60 min → 6° per minute.</p><p>Hour hand moves 30° in 60 min → 0.5° per minute.</p><p>Relative speed of minute hand over hour hand = 6 − 0.5 = 5.5° per minute.</p><p>Both hands coincide every 720/11 minutes ≈ 65.45 minutes.</p><p>Both hands are at 90° apart: 720/11 × (n ± 1/4) [complex formula — use direct calculation]</p><p>ANGLE FORMULA:</p><p>θ = |30H − 5.5M| where H = hours, M = minutes</p><p>If θ &gt; 180°, actual angle = 360° − θ</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6hx95a5",
      "content": "<strong>Ex.1 </strong>Find the angle between clock hands at 3:40."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ib2lj2l",
      "content": "<strong>Sol. </strong><em>θ = |30×3 − 5.5×40| = |90 − 220| = |−130| = 130°. Ans: 130°</em>"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "z1ecosp",
      "content": "<strong>Ex.2 </strong>Find angle at 6:30."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "qex5je9",
      "content": "<strong>Sol. </strong><em>θ = |30×6 − 5.5×30| = |180 − 165| = 15°. Ans: 15°</em>"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "8wgzjh6",
      "content": "<strong>Ex.3 </strong>At what time between 3 and 4 o'clock are the hands together?"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "uw9b3e6",
      "content": "<strong>Sol. </strong><em>At 3:00, minute hand is 15 min behind hour hand (= 90°). Time to gain 90° = 90/5.5 = 16.36 min = 16 min 21.8 sec. So hands meet at 3:16:21. Ans: 16 4/11 min past 3</em>"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ry6mlem",
      "content": "<strong>Ex.4 </strong>At what time between 4 and 5 are the hands at right angles (first time)?"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2x7w0c7",
      "content": "<strong>Sol. </strong><em>At 4:00, hour hand is at 20 minutes position. To be 15 minutes ahead (90°): 15−20=−5 (already passed). For next 90°: need to gain 15 min. Minute hand needs to close 20 min gap and then create 15 min gap = 35 min gain. 35/5.5 = 350/11 = 31 9/11 min. So at 4h 31 9/11 min. Ans: 31 9/11 min past 4</em>"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "t7y6ach",
      "content": "<strong>12.2  Calendar Problems</strong>"
    },
    {
      "id": "78u11t8",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>ODD DAYS CONCEPT</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Ordinary year = 365 days = 52 weeks + 1 day → 1 ODD DAY</p><p>Leap year = 366 days = 52 weeks + 2 days → 2 ODD DAYS</p><p>100 years = 76 ordinary + 24 leap = 76×1 + 24×2 = 76+48 = 124 = 17 weeks + 5 days → 5 ODD DAYS</p><p>200 years → 5+5=10 → 10−7=3 ODD DAYS</p><p>300 years → 5+5+5=15 → 15−14=1 ODD DAY</p><p>400 years → 5+5+5+6=21 → 21−21=0 ODD DAYS (400th year is special leap year)</p><p>DAY CODES: Sunday=0, Monday=1, Tuesday=2, Wednesday=3, Thursday=4, Friday=5, Saturday=6</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
