    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "pc9xl4b",
      "content": "<strong>Ex.5 </strong>January 1, 2000 was a Saturday. What day was January 1, 2001?"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "cwhmka0",
      "content": "<strong>Sol. </strong><em>2000 is a leap year → 2 odd days. Saturday + 2 = Monday. Ans: Monday</em>"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "sks3mjy",
      "content": "<strong>Ex.6 </strong>If 15 August 2020 was Saturday, what day was 26 January 2021?"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "t07f0pe",
      "content": "<strong>Sol. </strong><em>From 15 Aug 2020 to 26 Jan 2021 = 164 days. 164 = 23×7 + 3. 3 odd days. Saturday + 3 = Tuesday. Ans: Tuesday</em>"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "lzpfdnf",
      "content": "<strong>12.3  Practice Questions</strong>"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6r6u5jz",
      "content": "<strong>Q.49  </strong>What is the angle between clock hands at 5:20?"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "ik6qy1p",
      "content": "<strong>  (a)  </strong>30°"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "mr4vrnd",
      "content": "<strong>  (b)  </strong>40°"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "1ahqe5m",
      "content": "<strong>  (c)  </strong>50°"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "8f3ld4k",
      "content": "<strong>  (d)  </strong>60°"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "16jf0yp",
      "content": "<strong>  Ans: (b) 40°  Hint: </strong><em>θ=|30×5−5.5×20|=|150−110|=40°.</em>"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "gau0n3x",
      "content": "<strong>Q.50  </strong>If 1st January 2023 is Sunday, what day is 1st January 2024?"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "f5rxsen",
      "content": "<strong>  (a)  </strong>Monday"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "u6ybe3r",
      "content": "<strong>  (b)  </strong>Tuesday"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "ioxswd3",
      "content": "<strong>  (c)  </strong>Sunday"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "nl2bakc",
      "content": "<strong>  (d)  </strong>Wednesday"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "thjyakp",
      "content": "<strong>  Ans: (a) Monday  Hint: </strong><em>2023 is not a leap year → 1 odd day. Sunday+1=Monday.</em>"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "qfr7ke0",
      "content": "<strong>Q.51  </strong>At what time between 2 and 3 do clock hands coincide?"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "wmpt7z9",
      "content": "<strong>  (a)  </strong>10 10/11 min past 2"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "0b68768",
      "content": "<strong>  (b)  </strong>10 min past 2"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "joqs2fd",
      "content": "<strong>  (c)  </strong>11 min past 2"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "z97biqx",
      "content": "<strong>  (d)  </strong>10.5 min past 2"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "u9g0loz",
      "content": "<strong>  Ans: (a) 10 10/11 min past 2  Hint: </strong><em>At 2:00 gap = 10 min. Gain 10 min at 5.5°/min → 10×2/11 = 20/11 of 60/11... time = 10×60/55 = 120/11 = 10 10/11 min.</em>"
    }
  ],
